# Rebasing vs merge

A merge creates a new merge commit that combines the histories of two branches.
git merge 

Pros
 -  Preserves the exact history of development.
 -  Easy to see when branches were integrated.
 -  Safer for shared branches because it doesn't rewrite history.
 -  Good for collaborative workflows.
Cons
 -  History can become cluttered with many merge commits.
 -  Harder to follow a linear sequence of changes.

 Rebase

A rebase moves your commits so they appear on top of another branch, creating a linear history.

git rebase

